    "show_share": true,
    "description": "At present, the  OpenITI / KITAB corpus  comprises 10,243 text files, 6,268 of which are unique titles. Such a large, and growing, number of texts makes quality control challenging. But at the same time, it is precisely this large number of texts that can be the basis for quantitative methods of quality control. In this blog, Dr Lorenz Nigst would like to briefly explore how we can make use of a large number of annotated lines of poetry for a simple quality check of such lines.",
